WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.698
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Newspaper Class, level four.

2
00:00:05.998 --> 00:00:09.385
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.685 --> 00:00:17.422
Unit twenty: ASEAN and Southeast Asia. Today you will add information about places, times and reasons with where, when and why.

4
00:00:17.722 --> 00:00:20.595
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.533 --> 00:00:24.871
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.717 --> 00:00:26.625
ASEAN.

7
00:00:27.617 --> 00:00:32.066
ASEAN means the Association of Southeast Asian Nations, a regional group.

8
00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:35.602
ASEAN was founded in 1967.

9
00:00:36.217 --> 00:00:38.799
Your turn. Say: ASEAN.

10
00:00:41.633 --> 00:00:42.321
ASEAN.

11
00:00:43.083 --> 00:00:44.224
Member states.

12
00:00:45.217 --> 00:00:48.667
Member states means the countries that belong to an organisation.

13
00:00:49.283 --> 00:00:51.132
The member states meet every year.

14
00:00:51.717 --> 00:00:54.868
Your turn. Say: Member states.

15
00:00:57.733 --> 00:00:59.094
Member states.

16
00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:01.083
Cooperation.

17
00:01:02.083 --> 00:01:05.348
Cooperation means working together to achieve a shared goal.

18
00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:08.193
Cooperation made the project possible.

19
00:01:08.783 --> 00:01:11.900
Your turn. Say: Cooperation.

20
00:01:14.767 --> 00:01:15.895
Cooperation.

21
00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:17.454
Summit.

22
00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:21.030
Summit means a high-level meeting of leaders.

23
00:01:21.617 --> 00:01:23.709
The summit ended with a joint statement.

24
00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:26.806
Your turn. Say: Summit.

25
00:01:29.667 --> 00:01:30.679
Summit.

26
00:01:31.417 --> 00:01:32.128
Trade.

27
00:01:33.117 --> 00:01:36.417
Trade means the buying and selling of goods and services.

28
00:01:37.017 --> 00:01:38.865
Trade between neighbours has grown.

29
00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:41.905
Your turn. Say: Trade.

30
00:01:44.767 --> 00:01:45.501
Trade.

31
00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:47.030
Region.

32
00:01:48.017 --> 00:01:52.152
Region means a large area of the world with shared geography or culture.

33
00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:55.017
The region includes ten countries.

34
00:01:55.617 --> 00:01:58.060
Your turn. Say: Region.

35
00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:01.750
Region.

36
00:02:02.517 --> 00:02:03.773
Consensus.

37
00:02:04.783 --> 00:02:07.921
Consensus means general agreement among all members.

38
00:02:08.517 --> 00:02:10.609
Decisions are made by consensus.

39
00:02:11.217 --> 00:02:14.020
Your turn. Say: Consensus.

40
00:02:16.867 --> 00:02:18.065
Consensus.

41
00:02:18.817 --> 00:02:20.004
Integration.

42
00:02:21.017 --> 00:02:25.547
Integration means joining separate economies or societies more closely together.

43
00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:28.684
Economic integration lowered costs.

44
00:02:29.283 --> 00:02:31.889
Your turn. Say: Integration.

45
00:02:34.733 --> 00:02:35.874
Integration.

46
00:02:36.667 --> 00:02:40.770
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:41.617 --> 00:02:47.775
Visal, a textbook says 'A summit is a meeting where leaders make decisions.' Why 'where' and not 'which'?

48
00:02:48.883 --> 00:03:01.584
'Where' is a relative adverb. It replaces 'in which' for places: the city where leaders meet. 'When' replaces 'in which' for times: the year when ASEAN began. 'Why' follows 'reason'.

49
00:03:02.683 --> 00:03:04.068
Can I leave the word out?

50
00:03:05.183 --> 00:03:17.765
Often yes for when and why: 'the reason (why) members agree', 'the day (when) they signed'. But 'where' is usually kept after a place noun. Say 'the country where', not 'the country which in'.

51
00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:20.594
Can you give an ASEAN example?

52
00:03:21.683 --> 00:03:31.319
'Phnom Penh is the city where the summit took place.' 'Consensus is the reason why decisions take time.' 'It was a time when members wanted peace.'

53
00:03:32.467 --> 00:03:34.629
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:35.483 --> 00:03:39.724
Grammar focus: Relative adverbs: where and when and why.

55
00:03:40.024 --> 00:03:41.187
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:41.883 --> 00:03:45.055
A summit is a meeting where leaders make decisions together.

57
00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:49.505
1967 was the year when ASEAN was founded.

58
00:03:50.417 --> 00:03:53.786
Consensus is the reason why decisions sometimes take time.

59
00:03:54.733 --> 00:04:01.960
Use where after a place noun, when after a time noun and why after reason. They replace in which / at which and make the sentence shorter.

60
00:04:02.717 --> 00:04:06.217
Be careful! Don't say: The city which I was born is big.

61
00:04:08.167 --> 00:04:10.480
Say: The city where I was born is big.

62
00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:12.802
Use 'where' after a place noun.

63
00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:16.287
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:19.030
ASEAN in Southeast Asia.

65
00:04:19.330 --> 00:04:24.441
ASEAN is a group of member states in Southeast Asia that cooperate on trade and security.

66
00:04:25.433 --> 00:04:31.380
1967 was the year when five countries founded it, and Cambodia later joined the family.

67
00:04:32.367 --> 00:04:36.352
A summit is a meeting where leaders discuss integration and sign agreements.

68
00:04:37.367 --> 00:04:43.418
Consensus is the reason why decisions can be slow, but it also protects the interests of smaller members.

69
00:04:44.433 --> 00:04:48.894
Cooperation in a region where millions of people trade every day brings peace and growth.

70
00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:54.129
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:54.983 --> 00:04:57.796
Siem Reap is a city blank many tourists stay.

72
00:04:58.096 --> 00:05:01.285
A, where. B, when. C, why.

73
00:05:04.833 --> 00:05:06.612
The answer is A: where.

74
00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:11.433
2025 was the year blank the summit took place.

75
00:05:11.733 --> 00:05:14.492
A, where. B, when. C, why.

76
00:05:18.033 --> 00:05:19.801
The answer is B: when.

77
00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:22.624
Choose the correct sentence.

78
00:05:22.924 --> 00:05:30.537
A, This is the reason why we agreed.. B, This is the reason where we agreed.. C, This is the reason when we agreed..

79
00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:37.539
The answer is A: This is the reason why we agreed..

80
00:05:38.683 --> 00:05:42.390
A decision that everyone accepts without a vote is made by blank.

81
00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:46.610
A, tariff. B, consensus. C, debris.

82
00:05:50.167 --> 00:05:52.619
The answer is B: consensus.

83
00:05:53.783 --> 00:05:57.199
According to the reading, in which year did five countries found ASEAN?

84
00:05:57.499 --> 00:06:04.671
A, 1967. B, 1999. C, 2015.

85
00:06:08.233 --> 00:06:11.731
The answer is A: 1967.

86
00:06:12.933 --> 00:06:15.934
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:16.783 --> 00:06:19.479
How does ASEAN membership benefit Cambodia?

88
00:06:28.283 --> 00:06:29.737
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:30.037 --> 00:06:54.925
ASEAN membership gives Cambodia access to a large regional market through trade agreements, which helps exports and investment. It also provides a place where Cambodia can speak at summits as an equal member state and work with neighbours on security, tourism and development. Regional integration builds peace and shares skills, which supports long-term growth.

90
00:06:55.225 --> 00:06:57.004
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:57.917 --> 00:07:03.727
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and relative adverbs: where and when and why.

92
00:07:04.027 --> 00:07:08.908
Today's value is peaceful cooperation. Share resources through patience and dialogue.

93
00:07:09.208 --> 00:07:11.919
See you in Unit twenty-one. Goodbye!

94
00:07:12.219 --> 00:07:14.929
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

